  <model metaid="meta_metoprolol_kidney" id="metoprolol_kidney" name="Metoprolol kidney model" substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Metoprolol kidney model</h1>
        <p>Metoprolol, alpha-hydroxymetoprolol and metoprolol acid are excreted in the
urine. The renal clearances are given relative to the glomerular filtration
rate (GFR) and scale with the renal function (<code>f_renal_function</code>): the
renal clearance of metoprolol is <code>METEX_f</code> times the filtration of its
unbound fraction in plasma (<code>fup_met * GFR</code>), the one of a metabolite
<code>&lt;X&gt;EX_f</code> times the GFR. The concentrations of the kidney model are blood
concentrations, the plasma concentration of metoprolol is the blood
concentration over the blood to plasma ratio <code>BP_met</code>; the metabolites are
taken to have a blood to plasma ratio of 1.</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
