    <listOfParameters>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="f_renal_function" name="renal function" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The GFR relative to the healthy GFR <code>GFR_base</code> (101 ml/min at 75 kg):
a measured creatinine clearance of X ml/min is the renal function
X/101. 1.0 is the normal renal function, below 1.0 an impaired one.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="GFR_base" name="glomerular filtration rate (healthy)" value="101" units="ml_per_min" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="fup_met" name="fraction unbound in plasma metoprolol" value="0.88" units="dimensionless" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="BP_met" name="blood to plasma ratio metoprolol" value="1.2" units="dimensionless" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="METEX_f" name="renal clearance of unbound metoprolol relative to the GFR" value="0.815230242660216" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The renal clearance of metoprolol is METEX_f times the filtration of its
unbound fraction, fup_met * GFR: 1 is filtration alone. 95-109 ml/min
of plasma (Regardh1974).</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
